$ promptfoo --help
Usage: promptfoo [options] [command]

Options:
  -V, --version                    output the version number
  -v, --verbose                    Show debug logs (default: false)
  --env-file, --env-path <path>    Path(s) to .env file(s). Repeat the flag or
                                   use comma-separated values for multiple
                                   files. (default: [])
  -h, --help                       display help for command

Commands:
  eval [options]                   Evaluate prompts
  init [options] [directory]       Set up a new promptfoo project with prompts,
                                   providers, and test cases
  view [options] [directory]       Start browser UI
  mcp [options]                    Start an MCP server for external tool
                                   integrations
  redteam [options]                Red team LLM applications
  share [options] [id]             Create a shareable URL of an eval or a model
                                   audit (defaults to most recent)
                                   
                                   
  auth [options]                   Manage authentication
  cache [options]                  Manage cache
  code-scans [options]             Scan code for LLM security vulnerabilities
  config [options]                 Edit configuration settings
  debug [options]                  Display debug information for troubleshooting
  delete [options] <id>            Delete various resources
  export [options]                 Export eval records or logs
  generate [options]               Generate synthetic data
  feedback [options] [message]     Send feedback to the promptfoo developers
  import [options] <file>          Import a Promptfoo eval JSON export or an
                                   OpenAI Evals JSONL export
  list [options]                   List various resources
  logs [options] [file]            View promptfoo log files
  scan-model [options] [paths...]  Scan model files for security and quality
                                   issues
  optimize [options]               Optimize one prompt against one configured
                                   provider
  retry [options] <evalId>         Retry all ERROR results from a given
                                   evaluation
  validate [options]               Validate configuration files and test
                                   providers
  show [options] [id]              Show details of a specific resource (defaults
                                   to most recent)
  help [command]                   display help for command
